W: 1. Lift Mac Cahir Og your face, broodin' o'er the old disgrace
W: That black Fitzwilliam stormed your place and drove you to the fern.
W: Grey said victory was sure, soon the firebrand he'd secure
W: Until he met at Glenmalure with Fiach MacHugh O'Byrne.
W:
W: [Chorus:]
W: Curse and swear, Lord Kildare, Fiach will do what Fiach will dare
W: Now Fitzwilliam, have a care, fallen is your star low
W: Up with halberd, out with sword, on we go for, by the Lord
W: Fiach MacHugh has given the word: "Follow me up to Carlow."
W:
W: 2. See the swords at Glen Imaal, flashin' o'er the english pale
W: See all the children of the Gael, beneath O'Byrne's banner
W: Rooster of a fighting stock, would you let a Saxon cock
W: Crow out upon an Irish Rock, fly up and teach him manners. [Chorus]
W:
W: 3. From Tassagart to Clonmore, flows a stream of Saxon gore
W: How great is Rory Og O'Moore at sending loons to Hades
W: White is sick, Grey is fled, now for black Fitzwilliam's head
W: We'll send it over, dripping red, to Liza and her ladies. [Chorus]
